{"ISBN:9780060664497":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780060664497","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL1426118M/The_words_of_my_perfect_teacher","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL1426118M/The_words_of_my_perfect_teacher","details":{"publishers":["HarperCollins Publishers"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["51679"],"librarything":["6140"]},"isbn_10":["0060664495"],"series":["Sacred literature series"],"lc_classifications":["BQ7662.4 .O72513 1994","BQ7662.4.O72513 1994"],"key":"/books/OL1426118M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL226933A","name":"O-rgyan-ʼjigs-med-chos-kyi-dbaṅ-po Dpal-sprul"}],"publish_places":["San Francisco, CA"],"pagination":"xliv, 457 p. :","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part23.dat:123642921:909","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:143696458:951","marc:marc_laurentian/openlibrary.mrc:617366267:1042","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part22.utf8:178225055:918","bwb:9780060664497","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-003.mrc:456932975:5272","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_034.bib.mrc:324501777:5692"],"title":"The words of my perfect teacher","dewey_decimal_class":["294.3/4"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 441-445) and index."},"number_of_pages":457,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["93037175"],"subjects":["Rdzogs-chen (Rñiṅ-ma-pa)"],"publish_date":"1994","publish_country":"cau","by_statement":"Patrul Rinpoche ; translated by the Padmakara Translation Group ; with a foreword by the Dalai Lama.","work_title":["Kun bzaṅ bla maʼi źal luṅ."],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL1895685W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"oclc_numbers":["28927876"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"A favorite of Tibetans and recommended by the Dalai Lama and other senior Buddhist teachers, this practical guide to inner transformation introduces the fundamental spiritual practices common to all Tibetan Buddhist traditions. The Words of My Perfect Teacher is the classic commentary on the preliminary practices of the Longchen Nyingtig - one of the best-known cycles of teaching and a spiritual treasure of the Nyingmapa school - the oldest Tibetan Buddhist tradition.\n\nPatrul Rinpoche makes the technicalities of his subject accessible through a wealth of stories, quotations, and references to everyday life. His style of mixing broad colloquialisms, stringent irony, and poetry has all the life and atmosphere of an oral teaching. Great care has been taken by the translators to render the precise meaning of the text in English while still reflecting the vigor and insight of the original Tibetan.\n\nA preface by His Holiness the Dalai Lama, insightful introductory essays, explanatory notes, and classic illustrations enhance this quintessential introduction to Tibetan Buddhist practice."},"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-04-08T21:23:00.233370"}}},"ISBN:9787540901387":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9787540901387","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL946329M/Sñiṅ_thig_sṅon_ʼgroʼi_khrid_yig","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL946329M/Sñiṅ_thig_sṅon_ʼgroʼi_khrid_yig","details":{"other_titles":["Fa yao dao du, pu xian shang shi yan jiao","Rdzogs pa chen po kloṅ chen sñiṅ thig gi sṅon ʼgroʼi khrid yig kun bzaṅ bla maʼi źal luṅ"],"publishers":["Si-khron mi rigs dpe skrun khaṅ","Si-khron Źiṅ-chen Źin-hwa dpe tshoṅ khaṅ gis bkram"],"subtitle":"kun bzaṅ bla maʼi źal luṅ","description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Text of Rñiṅ-ma-pa doctrine for the Rdzogs-chen practice."},"isbn_10":["7540901381"],"series":["Khams kyi mkhas dbaṅ grags can dpe tshogs = Kang qu ming ren ming zhu xuan cong shu","Kang qu ming ren ming zhu xuan cong shu."],"lc_classifications":["BQ7662.4 O725 1989"],"latest_revision":3,"key":"/books/OL946329M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL226